# SIGN_HOST's header policy (Cloudflare Pages _headers, one rule for every path). The CSP and Integrity-Policy are
# the wallet paper's block (2.7) with HELPER_HOST and RPC_A, RPC_B, RPC_C put in, plus font-src 'self' (app.md finding 1)
# and the Solana trade's provider A and send paths (card signpage-solana-trade), and the origin of every provider in the
# kit's EVM venue lists (card page-evm-rpc-csp, read from the kit by scripts/live-checks/page-evm-rpc-csp.mjs);
# the other headers are the app paper's SIGN_HOST column (2.3). SIGN_HOST is the top window and frames APP_HOST (card
# signpage-shell): no page may frame it, its one frame is APP_HOST, and it asks for its own agent cluster. No
# X-Frame-Options (the CSP says it) and no COEP (it would make the APP_HOST frame need CORP and COEP of its own). The
# deploy script (packages/signpage/scripts/deploy.mjs) refuses an upload whose copy of this file breaks the policy.
# The prover runs here (card signpage-prover-host): its worker gets its own policy too (wallet.md W:880), which Pages
# joins to the /* rule's with a comma, so the worker runs under both at once; the setup files at
# /assets/zk/<sha256>.<ext> never change under one name, so they are cached for good (vault.md 2.14).
# The worker proves on its own threads (card signpage-prover-threads), each started from /prover-thread.js, snarkjs's own
# thread code as one pinned same-origin file, never from a data: or blob: URL, which worker-src 'self' refuses. The
# thread file gets its own policy too, joined to the /* rule's: it runs wasm and loads, fetches and starts nothing.
# The restore walks its deposit indices in Workers started from /walk-worker.js (card restore-shows-the-balance-in-seconds),
# one pinned same-origin module made a TrustedScriptURL by the page's policy walk-worker; its own policy, joined to the
# site's, lets it fetch and start nothing: it computes only.
# Permissions-Policy denies the APP_HOST frame (and this page) every feature it does not need; the frame has no `allow`
# attribute, so clipboard-write=(self) already keeps the clipboard API from it and the default 'self' kept fullscreen
# from it. fullscreen=() and picture-in-picture=() (whose default is every origin) say it outright (card
# signing-views-open-over-the-app: a frame under a sheet must not float a window over it).
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; worker-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://ct-api.unrealized.trade https://1click.chaindefuser.com https://rpc.mainnet.fastnear.com https://rpc.mainnet.near.org https://near.drpc.org https://archival-rpc.mainnet.near.org https://archival-rpc.mainnet.fastnear.com https://solana-rpc.publicnode.com https://solana.api.pocket.network https://public.rpc.solanavibestation.com https://sender.helius-rpc.com https://mainnet.block-engine.jito.wtf https://api.mainnet-beta.solana.com https://base-rpc.publicnode.com https://base-mainnet.public.blastapi.io https://mainnet.base.org https://base.api.pocket.network https://base.gateway.tenderly.co https://base.rpc.blxrbdn.com https://rpc.sentio.xyz https://robinhood-rpc.publicnode.com https://robinhood.drpc.org https://rpc.mainnet.chain.robinhood.com https://robinhood.rpc.blxrbdn.com https://rpc-robinhood.globalstake.io https://robinhood.api.pocket.network https://robinhood.daybreak-rpc.network; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; frame-src https://ct-app.unrealized.trade; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; object-src 'none'; require-trusted-types-for 'script'; trusted-types prover-worker walk-worker
  Integrity-Policy: blocked-destinations=(script)
  Origin-Agent-Cluster: ?1
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), autoplay=(), bluetooth=(), camera=(), clipboard-read=(), clipboard-write=(self), display-capture=(), fullscreen=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), hid=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), picture-in-picture=(), publickey-credentials-create=(self), publickey-credentials-get=(self), serial=(), usb=(), xr-spatial-tracking=()
# An outside app built on @blindfill/kit opens SIGN_HOST at /connect in a popup (window.open; card
# signpage-answers-outside-apps), and the page answers it through window.opener. COOP same-origin, which /* sets, gives a
# page opened by a cross-origin opener a browsing context group of its own and cuts window.opener, so /connect is served
# Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: unsafe-none. Pages applies every matching rule in file order and joins a header two rules
# set with a comma ("same-origin, unsafe-none", which a browser does not read as unsafe-none), so this rule, after /*,
# first detaches /*'s COOP (! Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy, as Pages' docs detach and re-set a header in one rule) and
# then sets its own. It touches nothing else: the CSP stays /*'s (frame-src APP_HOST alone, frame-ancestors 'none'),
# and /*'s other headers apply. The one risk it takes: /connect shares a browsing context group with its opener, so the
# opener keeps a handle to this window (navigate it, see when it closes) and the page is not process-isolated from it
# by COOP. The deploy script refuses any other /connect rule, and the live check signpage-answers-outside-apps reads
# both answers after each deploy.
/connect
  ! Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: unsafe-none
/prover-worker.js
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; connect-src 'self'
/prover-thread.js
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'wasm-unsafe-eval'
/walk-worker.js
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'
/assets/zk/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
